---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import ToggleDemo from '../../components/ToggleDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Toggle" description="A two-state button for text styles, filters, and view options.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Toggle</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">A button that stays on or off. Use it to turn on a text style, a filter, or a view option.</p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <ToggleDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Toggle usage"
      code={`import { Toggle } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/toggle";

<Toggle aria-label="Bold" defaultPressed>
  <Bold />
</Toggle>

const [starred, setStarred] = useState(false);

<Toggle variant="outline" size="sm" pressed={starred} onPressedChange={setStarred}>
  <Star data-icon="inline-start" />
  Starred
</Toggle>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass <code>pressed</code> and <code>onPressedChange</code> to control the toggle, or <code>defaultPressed</code>{' '}
      to let it keep its own state. While on, it has
      <code>aria-pressed="true"</code> and
      <code>data-pressed</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> is <code>"default"</code> (no border) or <code>"outline"</code> (a control border).{' '}
      <code>size</code> is <code>"sm"</code> (28px, 12px text),
      <code>"md"</code> (32px, the default), or <code>"lg"</code> (36px). Each size is at least as wide as it is tall,
      with 10px side padding.
    </p>
    <p>
      Icons are 16px (14px in <code>sm</code>) unless they set their own size. Mark a leading or trailing icon with{' '}
      <code>data-icon="inline-start"</code>
      or <code>"inline-end"</code> to tighten padding on that side.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>disabled</code> blocks presses and dims the toggle. Set
      <code>aria-invalid</code> to draw a danger border, and <code>aria-busy</code> while a change saves. The toggle
      also takes Base UI props such as
      <code>value</code>, <code>render</code>, <code>nativeButton</code>, and state functions for <code>className</code>
      .
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">toggleVariants</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Style a Base UI toggle"
      code={`import { Toggle } from "@base-ui/react/toggle";
import { ToggleGroup } from "@base-ui/react/toggle-group";
import { toggleVariants } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/toggle";

<ToggleGroup aria-label="Time range" defaultValue={["30d"]}>
  <Toggle value="7d" className={toggleVariants({ variant: "outline", size: "sm" })}>
    7d
  </Toggle>
  <Toggle value="30d" className={toggleVariants({ variant: "outline", size: "sm" })}>
    30d
  </Toggle>
</ToggleGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>toggleVariants({'{ variant, size, className }'})</code> returns the class names of a toggle. Use it when you
      build your own group or render another element as a toggle. For a ready-made group, use
      <a href="/components/toggle-group/">Toggle Group</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Toggle renders a <code>button</code> with <code>aria-pressed</code>. Tab moves focus to it, and Space or Enter
      presses it. A focused toggle shows a 2px focus ring. An icon-only toggle needs an <code>aria-label</code>. Keep
      the label the same when the state changes; screen readers already announce on or off.
    </p>
    <p>
      Color changes take 120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested. In forced colors mode the toggle gets a border
      and the pressed toggle is highlighted.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Off uses <code>--sprout-muted</code>, and hover uses <code>--sprout-hover</code>. On uses{' '}
      <code>--sprout-primary</code> on <code>--sprout-primary-subtle</code>, so the opt-in TulipFarm theme tints it
      green. Outline uses <code>--sprout-input</code> and <code>--sprout-surface</code>. Invalid uses{' '}
      <code>--sprout-danger</code>. Radius follows <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
